  "summary_en": "Rwanda's binding Special Regulations (Feb 2026) on unmanned aircraft systems, Part 27 of the Civil Aviation Regulations. It sets risk-based basic and specific categories, registration, remote pilot licensing, operator certificates, manufacturer declarations, training organisations, BVLOS and highly automated operations, UTM, security, insurance and privacy.",
  "key_provisions_or_claims": [
   "Two-tier categorisation: basic operations (notification) and specific operations (authorization, registration, pilot licence).",
   "BVLOS requires authorization after air and ground risk assessment, with detect-and-avoid and C2 link requirements.",
   "Highly automated UAS operations need consultation with the National Civil Aviation Security Committee; operator is responsible for oversight.",
   "UAS operator certificates require a safety management system, record retention and continued airworthiness reporting.",
   "Manufacturers must submit declarations of compliance; Authority issues acceptance letters; accident reporting within 24 hours."
  ],
